    "notes": "MODEL: mid-cycle owner-FCF DCF, component build (dcf-methods routing row 'operating company, cyclical'). COP is a pure-play upstream price-taker; single-year FCF swings 18.2bn (FY22) to 0.1bn (FY20) on the oil price, so FY0 is FY2025 (~$65 WTI, close to the $65-70 mid-cycle deck) and the driver paths do NOT extrapolate the 2026 oil rally that lifted H1-2026 revenue +14% YoY. FY2025 calibration: pretax 12,656 + interest and debt expense 855 + DD&A 11,500 - interest income 311 + SBC 336 = adj EBITDA 25,036 (42.5%); DD&A 19.5%; capex and investments 12,553 (21.3%); cash taxes 4,822 (36.5% of EBIT; FY23 33%, FY24 26%). Capex for FY2023-FY2025 and H1-2026 was missing from core_metrics (custom cop: XBRL tag) and was backfilled via make fix from the 10-K/10-Q cash flow statements. Terminal cap 12x (cyclical, depleting reserve base), Gordon at 9%/1.5% would be ~13.5x, so the cap binds in base.",
